    "updated_at": "2021-12-02T16:14:26Z",
    "body": "zsh and zle is an abomination, you probably know better than me honestly. Does starship have some sort of session storage it could use to mark it as already executed? It presumably has some sort of tracking between commands in order to display/know the elapsed time to begin with - so it should be able to track its own executions in relation to that?",
