    "updated_at": "2021-12-02T16:35:12Z",
    "body": "I would love that solution. Unfortunately, starship (by design) is essentially completely stateless. Any information that needs to be passed between draws (like commmand duration) is handled by the shell--the basic idea is to use `time` to get the system clock in millis, store that value into an envar, then check it again on completion of the command and pass that information into starship for rendering.\r\n\r\nI'll see if I can do some digging around this weekend (no promises though--I'm pretty backlogged at the moment!). If anyone else knows how other zsh frameworks handle this problem, I'd love to accept a PR to fix.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
